API.md §4.4 F12, ERRORS.md §1.5 (`source`), TYPES.md §6.2, §7.2: a part of a stored value checked against a part of its declared type names that declaration: a match arm, either side of `??`, the element of a list comprehension, the key and value of a map comprehension. These parts are checked against what the value is, so the note stays when the declaration's type reaches them through the value.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A kind.
enum K { a, b }

local let k: K = a

local let arm: UInt8 = match k {
  a => 1
  b => 256
}

local let opt: UInt8? = none

local let fall: UInt8 = opt ?? 257

local let left: UInt8 = 263 ?? 1

local let comp: [UInt8] = [258 for x in [1, 2]]

local let mcomp: {UInt8: UInt8} = {259: 260 for x in [1]}
-- findings.txt --
error[E3201]  a/a.canon:10:8
  256 does not fit UInt8
  expected by a/a.canon:8 (arm: UInt8)

error[E3201]  a/a.canon:15:32
  257 does not fit UInt8
  expected by a/a.canon:15 (fall: UInt8)

error[E3201]  a/a.canon:17:25
  263 does not fit UInt8
  expected by a/a.canon:17 (left: UInt8)

warning[W3401]  a/a.canon:17:25
  263 is never none: ?? has no effect

error[E3201]  a/a.canon:19:28
  258 does not fit UInt8
  expected by a/a.canon:19 (comp: [UInt8])

error[E3201]  a/a.canon:21:36
  259 does not fit UInt8
  expected by a/a.canon:21 (mcomp: {UInt8: UInt8})

error[E3201]  a/a.canon:21:41
  260 does not fit UInt8
  expected by a/a.canon:21 (mcomp: {UInt8: UInt8})

6 errors, 1 warning in 1 package (…)
